                            <comment id="18019308" author="JIRAUSER298472" created="Wed, 10 Sep 2025 07:58:43 +0000"  >&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;RootCause&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Root Cause&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Currently, partition refresh is directly executed by the KE query engine Sparder, without submitting a job.&lt;br/&gt;
As a result, there is no job-level overlap detection for the job_range.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name=&quot;DevDesign&quot;&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Dev Design&lt;/h2&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Adjust the logic of partition refresh to follow the normal job submission flow.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Partition refresh will submit a job, and the corresponding time partition will occupy the job_range, consistent with the handling of build/refresh jobs.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The job UI will display the refreshed partition range for better visibility.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
